From f8a86a7192597e863b68f353ebce9850eac5dc82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiron Builder <builder@chiron.local>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:11:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: Chiron: describe the GIC virtual interface ranges

KVM needs the virtual CPU interface and the virtual interface control block
mapped, not just the distributor and the physical CPU interface the SoC
description carries. Without them kvm_arch_init fails on this board and
/dev/kvm is never created, so the built-in KVM has no entry point a guest
could use.

The ranges match the GIC layout of the T7C: distributor at 0xfff01000, CPU
interface at 0xfff02000, GICH at 0xfff04000 and GICV at 0xfff06000, each
16 KiB except the distributor's 4 KiB. They go in the board file rather than
mesont7c.dtsi because the boards described by that dtsi have no reason to
carry a virtual interface they never use.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
index 6957fb1..c1b5d2e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/chiron.dts
@@ -2281,3 +2281,19 @@
 &eth_phy {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
+
+/*
+ * The SoC description gives the GIC its distributor and CPU interface only,
+ * which is all a non-virtualised boot needs. KVM also maps the virtual CPU
+ * interface (GICV) and the virtual interface control block (GICH), and with
+ * those ranges missing the hypervisor initialisation fails: /dev/kvm never
+ * appears and there is no way to start a guest. Describe the two extra
+ * regions here rather than in the shared T7C dtsi, where the boards that do
+ * not host guests would carry them for nothing.
+ */
+&gic {
+	reg = <0x0 0xfff01000 0 0x1000>,
+	      <0x0 0xfff02000 0 0x2000>,
+	      <0x0 0xfff04000 0 0x2000>,
+	      <0x0 0xfff06000 0 0x2000>;
+};
